# This project lives under ~/Documents, which macOS syncs via iCloud Drive.
# iCloud materializes " 2"/" 3"/... conflict copies of files that were being
# written while a sync pass ran — these are junk, never intentional. Ignored
# so a mistimed `git add -A` can never pick one up. Moving the repo outside
# an iCloud-synced folder is the real fix; this is just a safety net.
